        "id": 204953,
        "name": "KateWalker",
        "username": "TakeWalker",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/takewalker/{size}/5677_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-09-29T00:20:28.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I had no idea/forgot this episode was coming, so I ended up taking an impromptu and unplanned walk this evening! Thanks for helping keep me in shape, Christopher and Adam!</p><p>Gotta say, I love the use of Miss Info's theme and the victory music instead of the usual musical cues. :D Those help this new Editor's Note thing stand apart from regular episodes. And on that note, definitely less exciting than an episode, but still fascinating and worth listening to.</p><p>If nothing else, I'm most pleased that they talked about their actual creation process some. That seems to be the one aspect of Sentinels Comics that isn't touched on often, and I can understand why, but seeing how Writhe started as basically \"this shadow villain Tachyon punched once\" is a great peek under the curtain.</p>",
