      {
        "id": 204963,
        "name": "Chaosmancer",
        "username": "Chaosmancer",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/chaosmancer/{size}/1977_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-10-01T20:20:22.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>But, at the same time, you are always you're own harshest critic and I'm certain Adam is not wrong on any of his critics of his work. He just sees all the flaws every time he looks at his work instead of all the good things he did as well.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Honestly, I think Christopher kind of gets to cheat in this department as compared to Adam. As the \"Story guy\" to a story that is largely nebulous and ill-defined at times (What exactly did Judge Mental say that pushed IDealist over the edge instead of sealing the break-up of the Sentinels?) almost all the minor details that make or break the type of crtique that Adam is applying to his art is invisible or non-existent.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I'm sure if this were an actual comic book company and we had pages of dialogue to go through, Christopher would be just as likely to bemoan how badly he did five years or more ago as Adam is. Adam just got stuck with the job that required more immediate detailing that can't be easily redone.</p>",
        "post_number": 31,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:34:12.359Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
